### 1554 — Protocol v1 resource limits: fixed constants + local caps, no wire exchange (TASK-260715-18owh7)
- DECISION: M0 uses fixed schema constants and unilateral local caps; nothing new on the wire beyond the existing `maxFrame` min-negotiation. Hello flag bit 1, feature bit 1, and message types `0x40–0x4F` reserved (unallocated) for an evidence-gated M3 limits exchange. Rationale: peer-advertised limits are unverifiable claims (local hard caps stay mandatory regardless), the datagram ceiling is HEV-pinned so negotiation has nothing to negotiate, and manifest-verified relay upload version-locks peer pairs. Full record: board outcome `TASK-260715-18owh7_decision.md`; awaiting review acceptance (proposed ADR-021).
- FINDING: Pinned HEV caps UDP-in-TCP copy buffers at `UDP_BUF_SIZE = 1500` (`hev-socks5-udp.c:26`); `recvmmsg_tcp` returns `-1` (stream-fatal, not a drop) when `datlen > 1500 − addrlen` (`hev-socks5-udp.c:203-206`). With ADR-020 keeping HEV unmodified, the relay→client reply path physically cannot carry a UDP payload above 1481 bytes (IPv6). This, plus unfragmented 1500-MTU egress, fixes `maxUDPPayload = 1472` as a v1 wire constant; raising it is an HEV-fork decision, not a protocol negotiation.
- DECISION: Baselines (all injectable, schema-owned floors/hard ceilings, fail-closed on out-of-range config): maxFrame [2048,65536] advertise 4096; maxAssociations 256 [1,1024]; per-assoc queue client 32KiB/relay 64KiB; aggregate/direction client 1MiB/relay 4MiB; control reserve 16/64KiB; DNS WRR 4:1; idle client 60s / relay 120s (RFC 4787 REQ-5 floor; client-first stagger shrinks crossed-expiry reopen race). `0x0005` split into violation (>1472, association-fatal) vs policy (lowered local cap, drop); `0x0006` edge-triggered per saturation episode.
